This repository provides a downstream SuperMimic implementation for UniLab.
UniLab and UniSim are separate upstream projects licensed under Apache-2.0.

The implementation was developed with reference to the SuperMimic reference
code in supermimic_vibed, whose MIT license and original copyright notice are
preserved in LICENSES/MIT-supermimic.txt.

SuperMimic paper:
"SuperMimic: Scaling Humanoid Whole-Body Control with One Differentiable
World Model", Qiayuan Liao et al., https://supermimic.github.io

CtrlZ deployment adaptation:
The model XML was adapted for MuJoCo 2.3.7: position actuators became limited
motors driven by Bitbot PD, legacy compiler compatibility was made explicit,
and IMU sites/sensors were added. Matching meshes reuse the existing repository
assets; four additional source meshes are stored beside the adapted model.
The policy and reference export tool imports the original source policy and
motion library; deployment preprocessing follows that source contract.
